# Project Architecture And Stack Rules

## Architecture
- Keep architecture simple and clean with clear separation of concerns.
- Organize by feature and keep modules small, focused, and reusable.
- Prefer composition over deep inheritance and avoid unnecessary abstraction.
- Keep UI, state/business logic, and data/integration concerns separated.
- Refactor when complexity grows; do not add patterns unless they solve a real problem.

## File Naming
- Use kebab-case for all new files and directories.
- Do not create PascalCase, camelCase, or snake_case file names.
- Rename non-kebab-case files when touching related code, unless it is risky or out of scope.

## Framework And Language Constraints
- Use Astro for app/page/layout structure.
- Use SolidJS for interactive UI components.
- Do not introduce React, Vue, Svelte, Angular, or other UI frameworks.
- Do not add non-essential runtime libraries when Astro/SolidJS native patterns are enough.

## Examples
- Good file names: `hero-section.astro`, `site-header.tsx`, `contact-form.tsx`, `theme-toggle.ts`.
- Bad file names: `HeroSection.astro`, `siteHeader.tsx`, `contact_form.tsx`.
